// GridSim web app: base settings for every environment (ASP.NET Core configuration accepts these comments).
//
// F05: neutral defaults. Nothing here names a real host. Single sign-on (Sso) is OFF unless a deployment turns it
// on, and every visitor is then anonymous (all pages stay usable). A deployment that joins an SSO estate sets, for
// example through environment variables:
//   Sso__Enabled=true
//   Sso__Authority=https://login.example.com
// together with the shared key ring (Auth__KeysDirectory), Auth__ApplicationName and Auth__CookieDomain.
//
// N086 / N087: site identity is configuration too. With no Site section the page loads no analytics, carries no
// host-specific metadata or footer links, and /.well-known/security.txt answers 404; Auth:ApplicationName defaults to
// "GridSim". A deployment sets Site__GoogleTagId, Site__AnalyticsScriptUrl, Site__ShareImageUrl,
// Site__SecurityTxt__Contact / __Expires, Site__FooterLinks__0__Text / __Url and so on.
// See docs/developer/deploy/README.md.
{
  "Sso": {
    "Enabled": false,
    "Authority": ""
  }
}
